From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?John=20T=C3=B6rnblom?= <john.tornblom@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:33:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/28] radv/ps4: the completion fence writes L2 back

The EVENT_WRITE_EOP that ends every submission set TCL1_ACTION_ENA and
TC_ACTION_ENA, as the amdgpu kernel's GFX7 fence does. Gnm's "write back
and invalidate L1 and L2" cache action also sets TC_WB_ACTION_ENA (bit
15), and on Liverpool the L2 is not written back without it: the
DolphinPS4/Crema RADV port (Crema v01.90, Donkey Kong Country: Tropical
Freeze) saw the fence signal while a storage image's stores were still
dirty in L2, the buffer was released, and the write-back faulted.

Every signal of a submission stands for its data being in memory -- a
host read, a buffer freed, a flip -- so the fence writes L2 back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Bb93U7uY5qVNuEcHDggEfE
---
 src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps4/radv_ps4_cs.c | 18 +++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps4/radv_ps4_cs.c b/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps4/radv_ps4_cs.c
index 4232a8f..e552961 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps4/radv_ps4_cs.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps4/radv_ps4_cs.c
@@ -314,9 +314,17 @@ radv_ps4_cs_annotate(struct ac_cmdbuf *cs, const char *marker)
 /* The completion packet: one EVENT_WRITE_EOP of CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_TS_EVENT
  * (event 20, index 5) that flushes the colour and depth caches, writes back
  * and invalidates L2 and the vector L1 caches, and only then writes the
- * sequence number's low 32 bits -- the packet the amdgpu kernel's GFX7 fences
- * are (gfx_v7_0_ring_emit_fence_gfx), and the one the gnm_submit sample waits
- * on. */
+ * sequence number's low 32 bits.
+ *
+ * The cache action is Gnm's "write back and invalidate L1 and L2" (0x38 in
+ * the field at bit 12): TC_WB_ACTION_ENA, TCL1_ACTION_ENA and TC_ACTION_ENA.
+ * The amdgpu kernel's GFX7 fence (gfx_v7_0_ring_emit_fence_gfx) sets only the
+ * last two, and on Liverpool that leaves dirty lines in L2: the marker could
+ * reach memory while a shader's stores still sat there, and once the buffer
+ * they were for was freed, the write-back landed in released memory (a GPU
+ * page fault the DolphinPS4/Crema port traced to this). Everything a
+ * submission's signal stands for -- host reads, a freed buffer, a flip --
+ * relies on its data having left L2. */
 
 /* RADV_PS4_TRACE writes a tag to the queue's trace slot with WRITE_DATA (which
  * the gnm_submit sample runs on the console) at the boundaries of a submission
@@ -350,8 +358,8 @@ void
 radv_ps4_completion_words(uint32_t *words, uint64_t marker_address, uint32_t value)
 {
    words[0] = PKT3(PKT3_EVENT_WRITE_EOP, 4, 0);
-   words[1] = EVENT_TCL1_ACTION_ENA | EVENT_TC_ACTION_ENA | EVENT_TYPE(V_028A90_CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_TS_EVENT) |
-              EVENT_INDEX(5);
+   words[1] = EVENT_TC_WB_ACTION_ENA | EVENT_TCL1_ACTION_ENA | EVENT_TC_ACTION_ENA |
+              EVENT_TYPE(V_028A90_CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_TS_EVENT) | EVENT_INDEX(5);
    words[2] = (uint32_t)marker_address;
    words[3] = ((uint32_t)(marker_address >> 32) & 0xffff) | EOP_DATA_SEL(EOP_DATA_SEL_VALUE_32BIT) |
               EOP_INT_SEL(EOP_INT_SEL_NONE);
